🚽 Test case: #193 -- a by-value struct/union member-access sub-expression
🚽 (`show(b.corner)`) can be passed as a struct argument, not just a plain
🚽 struct variable. The member's blob lives inside the enclosing struct in
🚽 the caller's scope and is deep-copied into the parameter like any other
🚽 struct argument. Also covers a pointer-base member (`show(pb.corner)`,
🚽 composing with #196) resolving to the real pointee's field, and by-value
🚽 independence (mutating the parameter must not touch the caller's field).
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};
gang Box {
    gang Point corner;
};

skibidi show(gang Point p) {
    yapping("%d %d", p.x, p.y);
}

skibidi bump(gang Point p) {
    p.x = 999;
}

skibidi main {
    gang Box b;
    b.corner.x = 3;
    b.corner.y = 7;
    show(b.corner);

    gang Box *pb = &b;
    show(pb.corner);

    bump(b.corner);
    yapping("%d", b.corner.x);
}
